     "*   `HSIZE`, `VSIZE`: Horizontal/Vertical image size (number of rays).",
     "*   `HFOV`, `VFOV`: Half horizontal/vertical field of view in radians.",
     "*   **Degenerate Up Vector:** If `world_up` is parallel to `forward`, the cross product for `right` becomes zero.",
     "*   **FOV Definition:** Sources disagree on whether FOV is horizontal or vertical.",
     "*   **Time Complexity:** $O(W \\cdot H)$ to generate rays for all pixels.",
     "*   **When to use:** Standard volume rendering, ray marching, and simple ray tracing where ideal perspective projection is sufficient.",
     "*   **When not:** When using calibrated real-world camera data with known intrinsics/extrinsics (use [Camera Matrix Ray Generation](2172-camera-matrix-ray-generation.md)) or when depth of field is required."
